1
00:00:02,207 --> 00:00:13,176
The best career advice is locked in hour-long videos. You can't search it and you can't cite it. So I built something that can.

2
00:00:13,176 --> 00:00:28,377
One corpus, six ways to answer over it, and one judge scoring all six on the same labelled questions. Here's what that looks like running.

3
00:00:28,377 --> 00:00:46,393
Ask how to structure a resume summary. Every claim carries a source you can open. This answer is self-graded — same model judges its own output, so read 0.87 as a hint, not proof.

4
00:00:46,393 --> 00:01:01,634
Six engines, same labelled questions, one RAGAS judge — faithfulness, recall, precision, latency, and token spend, all lined up in this tagged run.

5
00:01:01,634 --> 00:01:18,946
Judged head to head on five questions — too few to crown a winner on a one-point margin. What is decisive is cost: the agentic loop burns eight times the tokens for no measured gain.
